 "caution_items": [
  {
   "title": "Small corpus",
   "text": "7.7 million words, versus hundreds of millions for the main languages. Frequency values are unreliable, so there are no frequency bands, only the all-words generators. The reference lexicon has 162,292 words, so generators, neighbourhood measures and cluster filters are rougher than for the main languages."
  },
  {
   "title": "Newspaper vocabulary added",
   "text": "50,929 of the reference words come from a newspaper corpus (Leipzig Corpora Collection, lav_newscrawl_2016_1M, 18.5 million words); 111,363 come from the subtitle list. Written sources are more formal than subtitles and contain more names and foreign words (151 probable English words were removed). Frequencies of the corpus-only words come from that corpus and are not comparable with subtitle frequencies."
  }
